The implementation is complete and fully validated. Here's a summary of the work:

## Implementation Summary

**`/workspace/submission/main.py`** — service entry point: adds the script directory to `sys.path` (for `-I` isolated mode) plus the vendored NetworkX wheel path, reads one JSON value per stdin line, and emits exactly one flushed JSON reply per line. All exceptions are caught so malformed input never terminates or resets the service.

**`/workspace/submission/wire.py`** — strict JSON decoding: duplicate object keys, nonfinite numbers and BOMs are rejected as invalid.

**`/workspace/submission/service.py`** — the persistent controller implementing PROTOCOL.md v3.0.0:
- exact schema validation for every op (exact field sets, integer-only fields with range checks, ID/owner patterns, list bounds);
- `load` with structural load relations and the overbooking check at *every tick and link* (later loads short-circuit to `ALREADY_LOADED`);
- `audit`/`advance`/`edit` with lease intervals, expiry, base-capacity edits, blocked witnesses (`used > proposed capacity`) and forced revocation;
- `prepare` with payload-bound identity, replay/conflict caching that precedes revision checks, the priority chain `stale → REFERENCE → TIME → WINDOW`, capacity denial and cut denial witnesses;
- `commit`/`cancel` with the exact priority orders (`MISSING/OWNER/replay/GONE/DENIED/stale`).

**`/workspace/submission/compiler.py`** — the schedule compiler:
- **plans**: weighted logical out-trees per demanded root, per-ordered-pair route counts that sum *exactly* to the logical edge loads, and a shared acyclic serial-route circuit (leaves per directed link, prefix-shared concat nodes) whose junctions only ever sit on ordinary forwarding vertices; every leaf occurrence is charged with the full multiplicity and checked against `p*b_l` per direction;
- **negative witnesses**: an exact min-cut search (Dinic) that finds a strictly deficient cut `Σ p·b_l(crossing) < Σ r_v(in S)` while guaranteeing the witness contains at least one but not all participants.

All arithmetic is exact integer arithmetic; the artifact is 8 entries / 122 KB (limits: 256 / 1 MiB), single-process, no network or subprocess use.
